\section{Mathematical Formulation}
\subsection{Ring-LWE Cryptosystem}
Let $R_q = \mathbb{Z}_q[x]/(x^n + 1)$ with $n = 2^k$. Secret keys and error 
terms are sampled from discrete Gaussian distributions. Ciphertexts 
$(c_0, c_1)$ encode astrophysical tensors using SIMD packing. Homomorphic 
evaluation circuits implement wavelet transforms, entropy metrics, and 
periodicity tests.

\subsection{Assembly Theory Complexity}
Molecular fragmentation trees are evaluated to compute assembly indices:
\[
A(m) = \sum_{i=1}^{k} w_i \cdot \text{frag}_i(m),
\]
where $\text{frag}_i$ denotes fragmentation depth and $w_i$ are structural 
weights. High assembly indices indicate non-abiotic molecular organization.

\subsection{Bayesian Verification}
Posterior distributions $p_t(\theta)$ are updated via Monte Carlo sampling:
\[
p_{t+1}(\theta) \propto p(\text{data} \mid \theta) p_t(\theta).
\]
Convergence is achieved when:
\[
\left\| p_t(\theta) - p_{\infty}(\theta) \right\|_{\text{TV}} < 10^{-5}.
\]

